  "id": "Compound::DB06216 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Asenapine is linked to Cyp3a4 through a series of molecular interactions that involve the enzyme Cyp3a4. The evidence suggests that Asenapine may influence Cyp3a4 through its ability to cause conditions such as Drug Withdrawal Syndrome Neonatal, Schizophrenia, and Blood Prolactin Increased, all of which are associated with the enzyme's activity. These conditions are mediated by other drugs, such as Prochlorperazine, Methylprednisolone, and Desvenlafaxine, which bind to Cyp3a4. The lowest common ancestor of these pathways is \"Agent Affecting Nervous System,\" indicating a shared biological role in the nervous system. The integration of these pathways suggests that Asenapine may indirectly affect Cyp3a4 through the activation of downstream pathways that involve the enzyme. The mechanism appears to be mediated by the nervous system, with Asenapine acting as a trigger for the expression or activity of Cyp3a4 via the binding of other agents.",
